* Simplified behavioural NE555, written for circuit-tutor (not the vendor model).
* Comparators at VCC/3 (TRIG) and the CTRL voltage, nominally 2*VCC/3 (THR); TRIG wins over
* THR as in the real part; RESET below 0.7 V forces the output low.
* Every function is smooth (comparators are 10 mV wide tanh steps), so the operating point
* converges without stepping. The latch state q (0..1) settles in about 0.1 us.
* Output high is about VCC - 1.7 V; the sourced current is drawn from VCC.
* Pin order matches the registry line: gnd trig out reset ctrl thr dis vcc
.subckt NE555 gnd trig out reset ctrl thr dis vcc
r1 vcc ctrl 5k
r2 ctrl lo 5k
r3 lo gnd 5k
* s: TRIG below VCC/3 (set), r: THR above CTRL (reset); TRIG wins. The comparators push a
* bistable (slope 10 at q = 0.5) rather than scale it, so q snaps between 0 and 1 and the
* circuit cannot settle half-way. RESET pin low forces q to 0.
bq qt 0 v = 0.5 * (1 + tanh((v(reset, gnd) - 0.7) / 0.05)) * 0.5 * (1 + tanh((v(q) - 0.5
+ + (1 + tanh((v(lo) - v(trig)) / 0.01))
+ - (1 + tanh((v(thr) - v(ctrl)) / 0.01)) * (0.5 - 0.5 * tanh((v(lo) - v(trig)) / 0.01))) / 0.05))
rq qt q 100
cq q 0 1n
* sharpened latch output for the output stage and the discharge transistor, so a latch that
* has settled at 0.99 does not leave the discharge transistor slightly on
bqs qs 0 v = 0.5 * (1 + tanh((v(q) - 0.5) / 0.02))
* output stage: high = VCC - 1.7 V through 10 ohm; sourced current comes from VCC
bout o1 gnd v = v(qs) * max(v(vcc, gnd) - 1.7, 0)
rout o1 o2 10
vsense o2 out 0
bsrc vcc gnd i = 0.5 * (i(vsense) + sqrt(i(vsense) * i(vsense) + 1e-12))
* discharge transistor: about 10 ohm to GND while the latch is reset
bdis dis gnd i = (1 - v(qs)) * v(dis, gnd) / 10
* quiescent current, about 6 mA at 9 V
rquies vcc gnd 1.5k
.ends NE555
